msgid "Booster Motor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:10
#: 807676184e9944bd9593e12ea42f5fe7
msgid "Copter 3.6 (and higher) and QuadPlanes support additional motors placed in the middle of the frame to provide additional lift.  This feature is compatible with any of the multicopter frame types (i.e. quad, tri, hexa, octa, dodecahexa).  The video above shows this feature used along with an :ref:`internal combustion engine <common-ice>` but the feature can also be used with electric motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:14
#: fbfcba5bba0149329e736049fbb79c91
msgid "Copter does not yet support horizontally facing motors to provide movement without leaning the vehicle (`enhancement request is here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues/10117>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:17
#: c7016d968ea24252b7bd8e913d2f393e
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:19
#: 32982a0dfe194aaf9f27e22f53728a74
msgid "Connect the booster motor's ESCs to one of the autopilot's RC Output ports (i.e. MAIN OUT 1 ~ 8 or AUX OUT 1 ~ 6)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:20
#: 23afccb548b74f76a9ab94fe14bf30a4
msgid "Set SERVOx_FUNCTION = 81 for \"Boost Throttle\" (where \"x\" is the servo output number)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:21
#: 95c2a468579a4dccaa4e3aaff197c02d
msgid "Optionally set :ref:`MOT_BOOST_SCALE <MOT_BOOST_SCALE>` to a value between 0 to 5 to scale the output for the booster based on the average output throttle sent to the standard motors.  A higher scaling factor will put more of the load on the booster motor.  1 will set the BoostThrottle equal to the main throttle.  The output to the main motor will always be between the ``SERVOx_MIN`` and ``SERVOx_MAX`` values (where \"x\" is the servo output number)"
msgstr ""
